FAILURES ROWS (key, status, detail) -- 1 row, the whole point of the cell:
  key    = security-0f3eb2ded85ad44b
  status = bot_check
  detail = ChallengeFailed: bot_check challenge_failed (bloomberg_press_and_hold)

THAT DETAIL IS EXACTLY THE SHAPE HVST-bx-3 PUT IN THE PIN. The form is
"<ExceptionClassName>: <message>" -- class ChallengeFailed, then the message -- at 70
characters, inside the 303-character cap, and it is NOT the bare word "error" that every
record before this pin carried. Measured, not eyeballed: the detail contains ':', it DIFFERS
from 'status', and it is non-empty, which are the three things the script counts as NAMED.
So NAMED=1 of FAILED=1: every failure in this record names its reason.

A TRUNCATED RECORD IS ALLOWED TO SERVE THIS READ, by the order's own words: "a truncated
record that DOES hold a failure still serves the read". STOPPED=bot_check is not an operator
stop and not a completion; what matters for AC1 is that the record ENDED and holds a failure
whose detail names a reason. Nothing here claims this cycle was failure-free or completed --
completed is False and it is recorded as False.

NOTHING WAS DRIVEN TO MAKE THIS PASS. No pair was planted or re-queued, nothing was signed
in, the task was not stopped, started or re-registered, and the state dir was never written.
The failure is the runner's own, from its own cycle, and it was read after the fact.

CONTROLS ON AC1'S REGEX, so the PASS is the record's and not the pattern's:
